{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:13:27Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 64, "kind": "message", "text": "That's sufficient confirmation \u2014 the spec's race-handling criteria are unaffected by this fix (the 404-swallow logic in the `catch` block is untouched, just now paired with a `finally`).\n\n## Handoff\n\n**Fixed:** `frontend/src/App.jsx` (all three review findings, same file, all in scope).\n\n1. **Blocking fix (flicker on natural expiry)** \u2014 `deferDelete` (lines 74\u201397): moved the `setPendingDeletes` removal out of the front of the `setTimeout` callback and into a `finally` block that runs after the `try`/`catch` around `api.deleteTask`/`refresh()`. The task now stays excluded from `activeTasks` for the entire duration of the delete request, not just until the timer fires \u2014 no more reappear-then-vanish flash on the default (no-undo) path. The existing \"no such task\" 404-swallow behavior in `catch` is untouched.\n\n2. **Toast stacking order** \u2014 `App.jsx:137\u2013143`: `UndoToast`'s `pending` prop now derives from `[...pendingDeletes.keys()]` (a `Map` preserves insertion order) mapped to their `tasks` objects, `.filter(Boolean)`-guarded against a task that's vanished from `tasks` some other way (e.g., a `Clear completed` race). This restores the \"oldest deleted on top\" guarantee from `docs/design.md` while keeping the round-2 crash fix (no `undefined` reaches `UndoToast`).\n\n3. **Optional purity cleanup** \u2014 `cancelPendingDelete` (lines 99\u2013107): reads the timer handle from `pendingDeletes` in render scope before calling `clearTimeout`, instead of doing it as a side effect inside the `setPendingDeletes` updater function. Removes the (harmless but StrictMode-flaggable) impurity the review noted.\n\nAlso updated the stale comment above the `pendingDeletes` state declaration (line 20\u201323) since it described the old tasks-filter derivation, which no longer matches the code.\n\n**Verified:** `npm run build` passes clean. `npm run lint` is blocked on approval in this headless session (same gap the prior developer and reviewer stages already hit \u2014 not something I can resolve from here). No frontend test runner exists in this repo (`package.json` has no `test` script, no `*.test.*` files present), so `npm test` per `CLAUDE.md` isn't currently runnable \u2014 that's a pre-existing gap, not something introduced by this change, and out of scope for this fix cycle.\n\n**Not touched:** backend is unaffected (spec calls for frontend-only implementation); no other files needed changes for these three findings.", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "97758105-17ca-4a7e-a40a-ad529b7e9589"}}
